{{define "credits"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Credits &amp; team · Counterfoil</title><meta name="theme-color" content="#014693">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/app.css"></head>
<body class="aboutpage">
{{template "pubtop" .}}
<section class="ab-band">
  <div class="ab-wrap">
    <h1 class="pubh1">Credits &amp; team<span class="enddot"></span></h1>

    <h2>Team Init to Win It</h2>
    <p>Sonal Verma (team lead) · Ashwani Yadav · Arpita · Vaibhav Gupta · Lakshay Bansal —
    VoyageHack 4.0, problem statement 2: an AI-native HR services platform.</p>

    <h2>AI disclosure</h2>
    <p>Claude (Claude Code) was used for research, drafting and writing this prototype's code under the
    team's direction. At runtime, the product's assistant runs on Google Gemini through typed, server-defined
    tools; with no key configured the product runs whole on rules and says so.</p>

    <h2>Prior art, credited</h2>
    <p>None of the building blocks is new to the world, and we say so: idempotency keys and intent logs
    (mycelium-runtime; Anchor, whose protocol write-up we also credit for attributable evidence and the
    three-valued verdict), request-bound signed approvals (the AP2 protocol; the counter-sign draft),
    read-back verification (SailPoint IdentityIQ), canary probes (Overpass), statutory deadline traces
    (Instanter), replay-gated activation (OneDecision), and the governed action flow sketched in TBO's own
    brief, as in fellow designs TBO-Helm, HireLoop and Karya. <b>What we add is the join.</b></p>

    <h2>Type and design</h2>
    <p>Montserrat, Open Sans, IBM Plex Mono and IBM Plex Serif, all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and
    self-hosted. The interface follows TBO's public product styling, measured from tbo.com and the
    TBOHolidays portal; no TBO logo or mark is used. Built with Go's standard library only — no framework,
    no database, no npm.</p>

    <h2>Honesty notes</h2>
    <p>Everything on the dashboards is measured from this instance's receipts — nothing is projected. Our
    design-spike numbers live outside this product and are labelled as spikes. We never claim "exactly
    once", "tamper-proof", "guaranteed" or "first".</p>
  </div>
</section>
{{template "pubfoot" .}}
</body></html>
{{end}}
